<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Marco Polo</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1254">1254</a>–<a href="/years/1324">1324</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Marco Polo was a Venetian merchant and traveller who lived in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a> between 1275 and 1292 during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yuan-dynasty">Yuan Dynasty</a>. He served at the court of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kublai-khan">Kublai Khan</a> and travelled widely in his realm. His account of his travels gave Europeans a detailed picture of Yuan China's wealth and cities.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/marco-polo.jpg" alt="Marco Polo" width="245" height="420" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Frontispice_%C3%A9dition_de_Nuremberg_1477_(cropped).png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
